(The proposed $5.8B take-private of Option Care Health, Inc. by Onyx Bidco LLC combines a $3.15B debt package with $2.873B in equity) Tj
T* (commitments, including a $1.4B minority co-investment by wholesale pharmaceutical distributor McKesson Corporation \(~48.725% of) Tj
T* (equity\) alongside Clayton, Dubilier & Rice Fund XII. The transaction contains no contractual financing condition and designates the Target) Tj
T* (an express third-party beneficiary entitled to seek specific performance of the equity commitments. However, the transaction architecture) Tj
T* (exhibits critical exposure at the intersection of syndicate structure and regulatory standards: equity commitments and the $291.93M Parent) Tj
T* (Termination Fee limited guarantees are several and not joint, leaving Option Care without recourse against the non-defaulting sponsor if) Tj
T* (either party fails to fund. Furthermore, while Parent is subject to a heightened 'best efforts' obligation for state healthcare and pharmacy) Tj
T* (licensing across Target's 86 pharmacies and 187 ambulatory infusion suites, antitrust clearance under the HSR Act is governed solely by a) Tj
T* (mutual 'reasonable best efforts' standard. Because Option Care sourced 68% of its supplies from four wholesale distributors in 2025 and) Tj
T* (57% from three in H1 2026, combining McKesson's distribution scale with Target's downstream network creates vertical foreclosure scrutiny) Tj
T* (that the Buyer Consortium is not contractually bound to resolve through burdensome divestitures under a reasonable best efforts threshold) Tj
T* (prior to the October 5, 2027 outside date.) Tj
